# Line endings for the data of record.
#
# Every extraction table is a CSV whose bytes are hashed into
# data/batch_ledger.csv, so a CRLF introduced by an editor or a platform is not
# a cosmetic difference: it changes the shard hash and makes an immutable shard
# look edited. Forcing LF in the working tree and in the index keeps the hash a
# statement about the data rather than about the machine that last touched the
# file.
*.csv text eol=lf
